<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Bias mitigation and language modeling performance: MLM loss, GLUE evaluation (Appendix Table <a href="#A1.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ A.9 Language modeling capability evaluation on downstream tasks ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ LLM Bias Detection and Mitigation through the Lens of Desired Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).
Results are averaged across five seed runs (<span id="S5.T1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DistilBERT</span>).
<span id="S5.T1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Base Model</span> refers to pre-trained MLMs. % drop indicates reduction in bias or MLM loss of fine-tuned model relative to <span id="S5.T1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Base Model</span>.
<span id="S5.T1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline</span>: <span id="S5.T1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AttenD</span>.
<math id="S5.T1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a statistically significant bias reduction. ALL: includes professions from all three profession categories.
<math id="S5.T1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>: training batch size.
<math id="S5.T1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>: weight is given to the old KL mean versus the current batch KL mean in adaptive loss, <math id="S5.T1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>: relative importance to MLM loss.
Values for epochs, <math id="S5.T1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.T1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> are those that yielded the best validation dataset performance.</figcaption>
</figure>
